{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1188741-help-me-understand-the-more-esoteric-parts-of-prime-resonance-and-the-rest-please","id":1188741,"title":"Help me understand the more esoteric parts of Prime, Resonance and the rest please","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-22T18:50:58-08:00","id":1188741,"title":"Help me understand the more esoteric parts of Prime, Resonance and the rest please","content":"So I'm in a game right now that has gotten to rather high levels of EXP. 30-35 and with a large focus on increasing our more metaphysical powers, aka: Magic. As such I'm playing about right now with Prime 5 after my previous Fate focused character has died, and I'm hoping to see if someone can help me understand the effects of Resonance, Leylines and Hallows as it were. I understand that everything has a resonance, as it were, and that said resonance is both indicative of the effects of people on a place, thing or otherwise, and in turn that resonance also affects how others feel about it in a kind of feedback loop process. Or at least that's my understanding of it. A knife used in a passionate murder carries resonances of sharpness, steel, knife, anger, murder, blood, etc. Of course the largest resonances and one that might overpower all of this would be knife, murder, anger, and so the ST would probably only describe this as the other bits are just trace elements. Leylines are just big &quot;rivers&quot; as it were of energy and often carry particular resonances too. And finally hallows are, what, breaches of particular note from the Supernal into the Fallen? Quasi-&quot;lakes&quot; of mana or essence? I understand the mechanics, but not really the flavor.<br /> <br /> So there's my rather poor understanding and knowledge elaborated, and so now I am going to ask questions that I can probably find the answers for in books and misunderstand things constantly, but hey, hopefully you can help fix that, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I understand if many of these questions are likely to be game or ST specific, but even just a general outlook would be helpful, or your own personal opinion too. Taken in bulk I can probably get a good general understanding of these things even with personal preferences in place.<br /> <br /> On the topic of resonance, how impact should it be, and how should it be described? Should an ST (or a player if given the option for exposition) state the varieties of resonances briefly before focusing on the important ones? How symbolic should it be, and should you flavor the appearance of a given resonance to the observer? Two people looking at the same car would sense the same resonance, but in two different ways? One would hear the rumbling of an engine and squealing tires and the other would simply feel a sort of smooth precision, oil and grease and cool steel, both implying &quot;car&quot;? And when I say impact I mostly mean how drastic of an impact on emotions or the nature of a place should it be? Should a bar converted to a violent resonance expect to break out into a fight in 5 minutes, or simply become known for being violent over the course of a few weeks as occasional violent events increase?<br /> <br /> I suppose I've come to realize that this is actually more of a question about Resonance, but it ties in a little at least. Okay, next awfully formatted and confusing paragraph: If there is a leyline or even just a building with a particular resonance, say, Peace, does that mean the region of that leyline or that building will generally be peaceful and feel peaceful? If yes, is this considered more the cause of the leyline being peaceful and making people feel peace which creates more peace for it? Or do people feel that way which fuels the leyline? Chicken or egg, basically. How does such a leyline form or change to a particular resonance? And are there any particular mechanics to these effects aside from the possibility of a +1 to casting if appropriate? Further, if I take that same peacefully resonant leyline or building and twist the resonance of it to the opposite, wrath or whatever, will that generally result in people becoming more wrathful and thus feeding the leyline more wrath and sustaining it? If I have a spell cast on it that only lasts, say, a month, before wearing off, would that Ley Line then immediately revert back to peaceful, or would the *forced* change simply dissipate and it would instead hold whatever resonance is most natural for it at that point in time at the end of the month, or would it perhaps revert to peaceful and then very quickly shift towards the dominant prevailing mood of wrath?<br /> <br /> <br /> On the topic of Hallows, how should one expect to find them, what are the likely effects of creating one, how should you try and describe them and how common are they? How valuable are they likely to be to the mage community, and then the rest of the supernatural community as a whole? Actually that's about it really. I understand the rest. Sources of Mana, often connected to leylines or ocassionally dormant if the leyline has moved on. Often spontaneous in genesis and destruction and very unpredictable. Most powerful ones in high places but can appear anywhere and ocassionally they are both Hallows and Locus and other supernatural special places. Produce Tass as appropriate to locale and resonance and their resonant mana can aid spells. I do wonder if the resonant mana you ingest should be considered to have an effect on your personality if you consume a lot?<br /> <br /> I think that's about all and I understand if this is difficult, annoying, vague, or otherwise problematic but I really would appreciate the help in improving my understanding and narrative descriptions of these things and their place in the larger world of Mage. Any and all input is appreciated and I'll be more than happy to clarify any questions needed to aid in this learning process so long as you're willing to tolerate it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T19:07:33-08:00","id":1188749,"title":"","content":"Usually, there is only one prevalent Resonance \u201ctag.\u201d What that is usually is ST dependent unless affected by a PC, unless a PC has set out to change it somehow. The Resonant tag will attempt to continue reinforcing itself upon reality. If you have a knife Resonant with murder it will continue \u201ctrying\u201d to murder, or be appealing to murderers. A Resonance ofSharpness doesn\u2019t necessarily carry the same connotations though, even if used to murder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T01:51:31-08:00","id":1188800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixelPuzzler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1188741-help-me-understand-the-more-esoteric-parts-of-prime-resonance-and-the-rest-please#post1188741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of resonance, how impact should it be, and how should it be described? Should an ST (or a player if given the option for exposition) state the varieties of resonances briefly before focusing on the important ones? How symbolic should it be, and should you flavor the appearance of a given resonance to the observer? Two people looking at the same car would sense the same resonance, but in two different ways? One would hear the rumbling of an engine and squealing tires and the other would simply feel a sort of smooth precision, oil and grease and cool steel, both implying &quot;car&quot;? And when I say impact I mostly mean how drastic of an impact on emotions or the nature of a place should it be? Should a bar converted to a violent resonance expect to break out into a fight in 5 minutes, or simply become known for being violent over the course of a few weeks as occasional violent events increase?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Changing the resonance of a place (a bar converted to violent resonance) wont change it right away. It will take time, once it starts generating essence with that resonance it'll attract spirits that eat that resonance and THOSE will eventually cause effects on the area around it as the spirits start to use their influences to perpetuate their essence source. Spirits are also created from resonance so it'll start spawning ickle spirits of violence if no spirits come along.<br /> <br /> Without spirits the violent resonance in the area might not even cause much change to mortals in the vicinity as most mortals cant detect resonance and on its own resonance doesnt alter people...(i think??)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T04:18:02-08:00","id":1188830,"title":"","content":"It does, but is very subtle. People would be slightly more prone to violence or the regulars will slowly change for people that fits the description.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T12:06:41-08:00","id":1188954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1188741-help-me-understand-the-more-esoteric-parts-of-prime-resonance-and-the-rest-please?p=1188800#post1188800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without spirits the violent resonance in the area might not even cause much change to mortals in the vicinity as most mortals cant detect resonance and on its own resonance doesnt alter people...(i think??)</div> </div> </div> </div>Without spiritual intervention an area's resonance has about as much impact as the sort of mundane factors that steer people towards one theme or another \u2014 think in terms of the effect your environment's paint job or background music has on your behavior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T14:18:48-08:00","id":1189008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1188741-help-me-understand-the-more-esoteric-parts-of-prime-resonance-and-the-rest-please?p=1188954#post1188954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without spiritual intervention an area's resonance has about as much impact as the sort of mundane factors that steer people towards one theme or another \u2014 think in terms of the effect your environment's paint job or background music has on your behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one of the best descriptions for this I've heard, Satchel.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In 1e, your understanding, oh OP, is utterly and completely correct. In 2E, it seems fairly similar, actually. The resonance of deep Mysteries and whatnot are currency that mages use to unlock their Gnosis, after all. (p94) Single <i>Ley</i> sources provide a single Resonance, but Nodes, being intersections of lines, <i>usually</i> provide multiple &quot;tags&quot;. Tass and Ley Lines only carry one at a time, but that doesn't mean objects in general are so limited. Essence has a primary form, too, but that is expressly complex. (You can declare that these &quot;tags&quot; are combinations of supernal concepts, already, and that's reasonable, especially for Essence.)<br /> <br /> Everything participates in the nature of what it is, rather obviously. It's a warped interpretation of Platonic Ideals: A thing will resonate with all the eidolons that define it, but it doesn't mean that resonance will spill into the areas surrounding it. The question of propagation isn't terribly well-defined, except as caused by ley lines, nodes, and hallows. Even there, the guidance is pretty brief.<br /> <br /> It's mostly ST call whether or not gathering a bunch of things that aren't particularly... loud, I guess ... into an area that share a resonance will have any effect on the local resonance at all. An unused-but-full gun cabinet could, I suppose, resonate with deadliness because its contents all do, but it seems more likely that it would be resonating with other themes.<br /> <br /> Similarly, a murder weapon certainly would resonate with murder, and the murder itself would provide Murder essence, as well. It's reasonable that it pollute nearby essence around it until justice is had or some other spiritually relevant rule ends the effect, but whether or not that Resonance, sitting on the item itself, directly creates an effect on the surrounding area's resonance is a Storyteller call. The essence a murder generates and the duodand possibly still carries or generates would certainly effect changes in the area. How much and to what extent, again, isn't clear. (The rules for possession are, in contrast, vastly more thoroughly developed and a related point.)<br /> <br /> If there are any guidelines in the Mage (or, for that matter, Werewolf) book, I'd certainly appreciate the heads-up. Otherwise, it's what many would hand wave with &quot;It's a Mystery, then, isn't it?&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's not <i>wrong</i>, though: Anything locked down in the rules requires more thought to alter than anything left vague. There are stories to be told where a murder weapon needs to be destroyed to get rid of a hideous feedback loop. There are other, very different, stories where avenging the murdered can right the wrong and actually reverse much of the damage, while still others might have a story where the mere tools have an effect only rarely and then weakly unless supernatural actors interfere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 02-23-2018, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}